==English==

===Etymology===
{{PIE word|en|tréyes}}
{{root|en|ine-pro|*steh₂-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|testifien}}, borrowed from {{der|en|fro|testifier}}, from {{der|en|la|testificārī}}, present active infinitive of {{m|la|testificor||I bear witness}}, from {{m|la|testis||a witness}} + {{m|la|facere||to make}}. See {{af|en|-fy}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtɛstɪfaɪ/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-testify.wav |Audio (Southern England)}}
* {{hyphenation|en|tes|ti|fy}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}} {{tlb|en|ambitransitive}}

# To make a [[declaration]], or give [[evidence]], under [[oath]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|author={{w|Ruzwana Bashir}}|title=The untold story of how a culture of shame perpetuates abuse. I know, I was a victim|titleurl=http://www.theguardian.com/society/2014/aug/29/-sp-untold-story-culture-of-shame-ruzwana-bashir|journal=The Guardian|date=29 August 2014
|passage=It was only after a decade away from Skipton that I was finally able to garner the courage to return and '''testify''' against my abuser.}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|Numbers|35|30}}
#*: One witness shall not '''testify''' against any person to cause him to die.
# To make a [[statement]] based on [[personal]] [[knowledge]] or [[faith]].
#* {{RQ:KJV|John|3|11}}
#*: We speak that we do know, and '''testify''' that we have seen; and ye receive not our witness.

